findings.description:
`testCacheIDPForLogin` inspects `IdentityProviderListQuery` contents but never asserts on the stream returned by `getForLogin`. The cached-hit path, the `idp == null` fallback (provider lines 247-250) and the in-transaction `isInvalid` path (lines 217-219) are therefore unverified. Scenarios not covered:
- creating or removing an IDP that does qualify for login (only the non-qualifying case is asserted);
- `ORG_ONLY`/`ALL` with a null organization, which is what `OrganizationAwareIdentityProviderBean` actually calls;
- changing `BROKER_PUBLIC`, `linkOnly` or `enabled` on an org-linked IDP;
- disabling an organization (the case behind the first finding);
- the new `idp.isEnabled()` re-check in `OrganizationAwareIdentityProviderBean`, which has no test.
